cels at). To get there I started working on a deterministic (as in no LLMs used) parser of queries that translates them to the Overpass QL.<p>Search queries are split into tokens and the algorithm tries to guess &quot;what&quot; you want to search and &quot;where&quot;. The former comes from a word list (known brands, sports, OSM tags) and the latter from the geocoder service (Photon).<p>You can get quite creative like &quot;cafes in Zurich by the Limmat&quot;, &quot;peaks over 4000 m in Valais&quot;, &quot;pharmacies open now in Bern&quot;. It's good for discovering hiking trails, e.g. &quot;hiking trails from Arth-Goldau to Rigi Kulm&quot;. It knows how to find stuff between two places, next to a place, near a place and so on. You can stack those as well like &quot;bridges over the danube in serbia 50 km from novi sad&quot;.<p>Except the search it has almost all of the features you would expect from a map like turn-by-turn navigation (Valhalla) with voice (Piper), public transport navigation in Europe (MOTIS), live traffic (only a few countries so far).<p>The app is GPL-3.0: <a href=\"https://github.com/cdutsov/hippomaps\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/cdutsov/hippomaps</a><p>I'm looking forward to feedback on searches that work or don't work for you + overall comments."}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Show HN: Fast deterministic natural language search for OpenStreetMap data"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://hippomaps.ch/?q=cafes+by+the+Limmat+100+m+from+the+lake+in+zurich#map=15.02/47.36708/8.54935"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_vihren", "story_50561199", "show_hn", "front_page"], "author": "vihren", "children": [50573821, 50574118, 50574122, 50574214, 50574335, 50574382, 50574488, 50574671, 50574746, 50575000, 50576579, 50577859, 50578179, 50578431], "created_at": "2026-11-19T15:16:02Z", "created_at_i": 1795101362, "num_comments": 30, "objectID": "50561199", "points": 105, "story_id": 50561199, "story_text": "I want to show you HippoMaps. It is a fully featured map and navigation app built on OpenStreetMap with a custom Overpass API engine for really fast search of POIs, areas and ways.<p>My aim with HippoMaps is to get to a level where I don&#x27;t need Google Maps anymore. The biggest hurdle IMHO with OSM based apps is the lack of nice and fast search (where GMaps excels at). To get there I started working on a deterministic (as in no LLMs used) parser of queries that translates them to the Overpass QL.<p>Search queries are split into tokens and the algorithm tries to guess &quot;what&quot; you want to search and &quot;where&quot;. The former comes from a word list (known brands, sports, OSM tags) and the latter from the geocoder service (Photon).<p>You can get quite creative like &quot;cafes in Zurich by the Limmat&quot;, &quot;peaks over 4000 m in Valais&quot;, &quot;pharmacies open now in Bern&quot;. It&#x27;s good for discovering hiking trails, e.g. &quot;hiking trails from Arth-Goldau to Rigi Kulm&quot;. It knows how to find stuff between two places, next to a place, near a place and so on. You can stack those as well like &quot;bridges over the danube in serbia 50 km from novi sad&quot;.<p>Except the search it has almost all of the features you would expect from a map like turn-by-turn navigation (Valhalla) with voice (Piper), public transport navigation in Europe (MOTIS), live traffic (only a few countries so far).<p>The app is GPL-3.0: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;cdutsov&#x2F;hippomaps\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;cdutsov&#x2F;hippomaps</a><p>I&#x27;m looking forward to feedback on searches that work or don&#x27;t work for you + overall comments.", "title": "Show HN: Fast deterministic natural language search for OpenStreetMap data", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T18:59:54Z", "url": "https://hippomaps.ch/?q=cafes+by+the+Limmat+100+m+from+the+lake+in+zurich#map=15.02/47.36708/8.54935"}, {"_highlightResult